{"Global manage check treats having only view permission as sufficient to manage groups, allowing privilege escalation where users with view-only authorization can perform manage operations": 0.9345740079879761, "getOrCreateResource method switches directly on resourceType without checking for null, causing NullPointerException at runtime instead of controlled validation error when callers pass null resource type": 0.8758400678634644, "getGroupIdsWithViewPermission method checks membership-related scopes (VIEW_MEMBERS/MANAGE_MEMBERS) instead of view scopes (VIEW/MANAGE), incorrectly omitting groups user can view from result set": 0.4344535768032074, "Test creates a persistent group that is never scheduled for cleanup, leaving test data in realm and causing later tests to fail intermittently": 0.12147863954305649, "Management check unconditionally grants full manage access to anyone with legacy manage-users admin role, bypassing authorization policy engine and disabling fine-grained user management restrictions": 0.4568581283092499, "View check always allows anyone with legacy view-users or manage-users roles to view all users, ignoring authorization policy configuration": 0.5633289217948914}